        "heading": "Guest Screening, Daytime Visiting Rules, and Curfews",
        "content": "\n          <p>Your room is your sanctuary for study, rest, and personal recovery. Never allow romantic enthusiasm to compromise your personal safety rules.</p>\n          <p>Enforce these four rules for off-campus dating:</p>\n          <ol>\n            <li><strong>The Three-Month Verification Benchmark:</strong> Keep early dating entirely outside your residence. Do not reveal your exact lodge location, room number, or compound until you have shared multiple public dates and verified their student standing.</li>\n            <li><strong>Daylight Only Visiting Windows:</strong> If you choose to host a partner for study or lunch, schedule visits between 11:00 AM and 5:00 PM when other lodge residents are awake and compound visibility is high.</li>\n            <li><strong>No Overnight Guests in Early Stages:</strong> Decline overnight stays during the initial phases of dating. Overnight stays in unfenced lodges blur personal boundaries and can lead to dangerous conflicts if an argument occurs late at night.</li>\n            <li><strong>Immediate Departure Boundaries:</strong> If a date becomes argumentative, sullen, or refuses to leave when requested, do not hesitate to contact nearby lodge neighbors or lodge executive officers to escort them off the premises.</li>\n            <li><strong>Preserve Domestic Boundaries:</strong> Do not allow casual dating partners to leave personal clothing, spare shoes, or toiletries in your room, which establishes an unintended expectation of cohabitation.</li>\n          </ol>\n        "
